"""
Aletheia v5.0.1 — Training Module (Fixed)
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

Single-file training infrastructure with strict section boundaries.
Each SECTION is self-contained within its declared dependencies and exposes
a clearly documented public API.  Navigate with:   Ctrl+F  "SECTION #"

Architecture
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  SECTION  0 │ Imports & Type Definitions
  SECTION  1 │ Foundation Utilities
  SECTION  2 │ Configuration Helpers
  SECTION  3 │ Danger-Aware Sampling
  SECTION  4 │ Replay Buffer
  SECTION  5 │ Rollout Buffer (PPO)
  SECTION  6 │ Loss Functions
  SECTION  7 │ Policy & Optimizer Utilities
  SECTION  8 │ Training Step
  SECTION  9 │ Imagination Engine
  SECTION 10 │ Data Collection (RolloutCollector)
  SECTION 11 │ Training State & Loop
  SECTION 12 │ Auxiliary Tools (Noise · Gradient · Router)
  SECTION 13 │ Validation & Statistics
  SECTION 14 │ Evaluation
  SECTION 15 │ Performance Benchmarking
  SECTION 16 │ Factory Functions & Exports

Dependency DAG  (S# → depends on S#)
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  S1  → external (foundation)
  S2  → external (config, foundation)
  S3  → S1
  S4  → S1, S3
  S5  → (standalone)
  S6  → S1, external (foundation)
  S7  → S1, S6
  S8  → S2, S6, S7
  S9  → S1, S7
  S10 → S1, S7
  S11 → S2, S4, S6, S8, S9, S10
  S12 → (standalone)
  S13 → (standalone)
  S14 → S1, S7
  S15 → (standalone)
  S16 → all sections (factory wiring)

Critical Fixes from v4.5
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  [BUG-1.1] obs filling moved INSIDE sampling loop (was outside → only last
            sample filled; all other slots contained uninitialised memory)
  [BUG-1.2] Separate optimizers for WM / RL / alpha via OptimizerBundle
            (shared optimizer corrupts Adam momentum with zero-gradient steps)
  [BUG-1.3] WM metrics recorded once, excluded from PPO-epoch accumulation
            
  [BUG-1.4] RolloutCollector stores terminal next_obs before env.reset()
  [BUG-1.5] _add_to_buffer uses explicit (obs, next_obs) pairs with proper
            episode-boundary handling
  [BUG-2.1] compute_entropy_loss replaced by compute_entropy_from_distribution
            (clear input contract: accepts a Distribution, not ambiguous tensors)
  [BUG-2.2] ModelWrapper raises on encoding failure instead of silent fallback
            to raw vitals (which would cause dimension mismatch downstream)
  [BUG-2.3] Entropy protection and adaptive alpha: target_entropy positive for
            discrete actions; warning if both enabled simultaneously
  [BUG-2.4] Imagination engine uses continue-head probability to truncate
            imagined trajectories
  [BUG-2.5] Removed numerically unstable "vectorized" GAE (pow overflow);
            recursive implementation is the sole default
  [FIX-REG] Danger function registry replaces hardcoded physics rules
  [FIX-VAL] extract_real_value() unifies CriticOutput → scalar value
  [FIX-NI]  NoiseInjector.enabled stored as plain Python bool
  [FIX-EXP] __all__ contains only public API symbols
  [FIX-IMP] Self-referencing _verify_imports removed
  [FIX-DOC] All public functions have complete docstrings
"""

